WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:03.570
-Hello, everyone, and welcome
back to my attic crawl space.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.371
We have been focusing a lot

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:08.941
on that mysterious
tiny little door over there.

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:11.544
And we're taking guesses
for what's behind it

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.946
at whatsupwithsethstinydoor
@gmail.com.

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:16.916
Again, it's very unlikely
we will ever check that account,

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.617
let alone read any of it
on the air.

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:21.120
But, you know,
what else are you doing?

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.357
Now, I've also noticed there
has been some speculation online

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.327
about another aspect
of our makeshift setup here,

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.962
"The Thorn Birds."

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:33.432
Of all the books in my house,
why did I choose to highlight

00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:36.669
this 1977 Australian romance
novel that was later adapted

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.272
into a hit 1983 television
mini-series?

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.508
Have I actually read it?
If so, why?

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:43.542
Am I secretly 78 years old?

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:45.411
Maybe I'm not actually
at my house,

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:46.613
but my parents' house.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.848
Or maybe I just want to prove
to everyone

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.051
that on top of being
a well-known bibliophile

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.685
who is up on the latest
literary trends,

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:56.588
I am also an old soul
who loves a steamy read

00:00:56.588 --> 00:00:59.258
about a torrid affair
between an innocent farm girl

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:00.993
and a hot priest.

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:03.129
Anyway, if you have any guesses,
send them

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.466
to whydidsethpickthethornbirds
@gmail.com.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:09.202
there is almost no way we'll
read anything you send us.

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.569
But you know, what the hell?

00:01:10.569 --> 00:01:12.505
You can either spend your time
doing that

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.508
or trying to recover the
password to your workout app,

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.777
giving up, and taking
a three-hour bath,

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.345
like the rest of us.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:22.114
And while are you're doing that,
the president and his allies

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:24.216
are trying to wish away
the coronavirus pandemic

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:25.518
and hoping you'll forget

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.886
that he badly botched
his response to the crisis.

00:01:27.886 --> 00:01:30.323
For more on this it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:34.360
♪♪

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.729
As we have seen throughout
his presidency,

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.731
Donald Trump is both an emblem

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.334
and an enabler
of a broken government.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.369
And that government
has put lives at risk

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:44.770
with its arrogance
and incompetence.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:47.306
For example, at one of his
daily press conferences

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:50.276
this week, as the U.S.
was continuing to face down

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.879
a deadly coronavirus spreading
rapidly throughout the country,

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:55.849
he bristled when the word
"testing" came up

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:58.751
and complained that it wasn't
the federal government's job

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.253
to test people.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:03.122
-Testing is still a big issue
in this country.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:06.892
When can hospitals expect --
-Put the slide up again, please.

00:02:06.892 --> 00:02:11.197
-When can hospitals expect
to receive a quick turnaround

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.965
of its test results?
-Are you ready? Are you ready?

00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:15.235
Hospitals can do
their own testing, also.

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.203
States can do their own testing.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:19.672
States are supposed
to be doing testing.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.041
Hospitals as opposed to be doing
testing.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.544
Do you understand that?
We're the federal government.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:27.179
Listen,
we're the federal government.

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:30.083
We're not supposed to stand on
street corners doing testing.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.685
-Trump thinks testing
happens on street corners,

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.154
because if he weren't president,

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:36.322
he'd definitely be selling
fake tests

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.823
on street corners right now.

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:39.192
He'd be set up in Times Square

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:42.728
with a bunch of Q-tips laid out
on a black folding table.

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:45.231
[ As Trump ] Who needs swabs?
We got your swabs here.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:48.067
What? No, lady,
they're not Q-tips,

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.370
they're high quality
medical swabs.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.871
Look, if you're not buying,
just move on.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.440
I got a lot of customers here.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.941
[ Normal voice ]
Also if you don't mind,

00:02:55.941 --> 00:02:57.276
I want to go back
to this part --

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:58.744
-Are you ready? Are you ready?

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:01.413
-It's such a dickhead move to
ask someone if they're ready,

00:03:01.413 --> 00:03:03.416
like you're about to blow
their minds.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:07.186
He's like a guy sitting at a
piano saying, "Check this out!"

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:10.423
And then pecking out
"Chopsticks" at half-speed.

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:12.291
I also love the sheer audacity
of this guy

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:13.626
asking someone else
if they're ready.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.929
Remember, Trump is the guy
who in just four years,

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:17.963
went from this...

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:20.132
-I alone to fix it.

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:22.301
-...to this.
-And we're backup.

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:24.003
Remember we're a backup.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.437
-Trump thought he alone
could fix it

00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:27.340
until he saw what it was.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.641
It's like when you used
to go on road trips

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.376
with your buds
and your car would break down.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.145
You had that one friend
who was always like,

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:33.546
"Hey, pop the hood. I got this."

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:36.015
And then you know,
just stand there for a while,

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.583
hands on his hip looking at it.

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.285
Then he'd finally say,

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:43.155
"Damn, there's a lot
of stuff under here.

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:44.490
You have AAA?"

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.293
And now, as the outbreak
continues to intensify

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.727
and the death toll mounts,

00:03:48.727 --> 00:03:50.363
NPR reports that
the federal government

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:53.599
will end funding for coronavirus
testing sites this Friday.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:56.935
In a few places, those sites
will close as a result.

00:03:56.935 --> 00:04:00.139
You think now is the time
to cut off funding for tests?

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.707
Are you insane?

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:03.242
It's like getting halfway
through surgery

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:04.944
taking the guy's spleen out
and saying,

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:06.812
"All right. You can wake him up.

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:08.447
He can sew himself back
together.

00:04:08.447 --> 00:04:09.915
That's the easy part."

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:13.585
And then today we learned
roughly 17-million people

00:04:13.585 --> 00:04:15.254
have lost their jobs
in just three weeks

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:17.389
as the death toll passed 15,000.

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:19.192
And yet, Trump is once again
rushing to pretend

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:22.294
this will all go away and hoping
people will forget that,

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:23.996
as we detailed yesterday,

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:26.265
he literally ignored
years of warnings

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:27.934
about the threat of a pandemic.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:30.602
-Ultimately the goal
is to ease the guidelines

00:04:30.602 --> 00:04:34.707
and open things up to very large
sections of our country

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.975
as we near the end
of our historic battle

00:04:36.975 --> 00:04:39.178
with the invisible enemy.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:41.647
There's tremendous hope
as we look forward

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:44.917
and we begin to see the light
at the end of the tunnel.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.885
-"Once we open up
our great country,

00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:48.587
and it will be sooner
rather than later,

00:04:48.587 --> 00:04:50.289
the horror
of the invisible enemy,

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:53.059
except those that sadly lost
a family member or friend,

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:55.127
must be quickly forgotten."

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:56.495
-[ Sighs ]

00:04:56.495 --> 00:04:58.664
I love that
"Hold a Grudge Jones" over here

00:04:58.664 --> 00:05:00.800
is telling us we have to
forget it and move on.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.270
The same guy who is still
so mad at John McCain

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.805
that he tweeted McCain
was last in his class

00:05:06.805 --> 00:05:10.275
at Annapolis
seven months after he died.

00:05:10.275 --> 00:05:12.678
This [bleep] is the same
as people who act terribly

00:05:12.678 --> 00:05:14.513
and then when you point out
their terrible behavior,

00:05:14.513 --> 00:05:16.349
cry, "What of civility?"

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:19.184
Civility isn't a right.
It's earned.

00:05:19.184 --> 00:05:20.819
And sometimes people
don't deserve it.

00:05:20.819 --> 00:05:22.955
Just like some people don't
deserve their bad decisions

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:24.656
to be lost to history.

00:05:24.656 --> 00:05:25.958
And nothing gives away the game

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:27.659
of how badly Trump
has handled this

00:05:27.659 --> 00:05:29.529
like Trump telling us now

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:31.330
we have to forget about it
when it's over.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.498
During World War II,

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:33.899
Winston Churchill
wasn't thinking,

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:35.768
"I never want to hear
about this again."

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.469
He was champing on a cigar
thinking,

00:05:37.469 --> 00:05:40.005
"When this is over, there
are gonna be a million books

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:42.174
about how hard I crushed
this [bleep]"

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:44.843
You know, or however
he would say it.

00:05:44.843 --> 00:05:47.312
Probably like this.
[ Muttering ]

00:05:47.312 --> 00:05:49.849
It would be like that, would --
[ Muttering ]

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:51.350
That would like, preface it.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.753
I mean,
who should all forget about it?

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:56.355
Trump is like an employee
at Wendy's who gets fired,

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:57.623
