00:10:15.414 --> 00:10:17.049
on LaserDisc."

00:10:17.049 --> 00:10:19.751
And then he claimed that
because his uncle was smart,

00:10:19.751 --> 00:10:22.187
his uncle was smart,

00:10:22.187 --> 00:10:24.456
he personally knew a lot
about coronavirus.

00:10:24.456 --> 00:10:25.490
-And I like this stuff.

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:29.028
You know,
my uncle is a great person.

00:10:29.028 --> 00:10:31.096
He was at MIT.
He taught at MIT for,

00:10:31.096 --> 00:10:33.299
I think, like a record
number of years.

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:35.601
He was a great super-genius.

00:10:35.601 --> 00:10:37.970
Dr. John Trump.
I like this stuff.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:40.505
I really get it.
-No, you don't.

00:10:40.505 --> 00:10:41.807
You look like you wandered

00:10:41.807 --> 00:10:44.142
into the middle of a press
conference from a tour.

00:10:44.142 --> 00:10:46.211
He should be holding a map
with a Nikon camera

00:10:46.211 --> 00:10:48.614
around his neck asking
the scientists for directions.

00:10:48.614 --> 00:10:50.249
[ As Trump ] You guys know
how to get to Times Square?

00:10:50.249 --> 00:10:54.387
I wanna buy some swabs.
I hear it's the real deal.

00:10:54.387 --> 00:10:55.921
[ Normal voice ]
So, you don't even know

00:10:55.921 --> 00:10:58.157
what your uncle taught
or how many years he taught,

00:10:58.157 --> 00:11:00.659
but you know he was
a great super-genius?

00:11:00.659 --> 00:11:03.161
Was your uncle Wile E. Coyote?

00:11:03.161 --> 00:11:05.264
[ As Trump ] Taught at MIT
for a record number of years.

00:11:05.264 --> 00:11:08.166
But he could never catch
the Road Runner.

00:11:08.166 --> 00:11:09.268
You know, he's the one
that told me

00:11:09.268 --> 00:11:11.203
there was a light
at the end of a tunnel.

00:11:11.203 --> 00:11:13.372
A real tunnel.

00:11:13.372 --> 00:11:17.142
Not one painted onto the side
of a mountain.

00:11:17.142 --> 00:11:18.678
[ Normal voice ]
That was the day that Trump said

00:11:18.678 --> 00:11:21.012
anyone who wants a test
will get a test.

00:11:21.012 --> 00:11:23.014
And now he's cutting funding
for testing.

00:11:23.014 --> 00:11:25.450
And I know he'd prefer it
if we were all Drew Barrymore

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.986
from "50 First Dates"
and we'd wake up every morning

00:11:27.986 --> 00:11:32.157
and say, "President Trump?
Oh, I'll give that a chance."

00:11:32.157 --> 00:11:33.892
But that's not how
most of our brains work.

00:11:33.892 --> 00:11:35.227
We remember the things
you've said

00:11:35.227 --> 00:11:37.529
and then we hold you to account
for them.

00:11:37.529 --> 00:11:40.432
It now it looks like our chance
to do that will be in November

00:11:40.432 --> 00:11:42.200
in a race between Trump
and Joe Biden

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:43.536
after Bernie Sanders officially

00:11:43.536 --> 00:11:45.270
dropped out of
the presidential race yesterday,

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:47.339
Which sucks for
a ton of reasons.

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:49.842
One of which is the timing
on Medicare For All.

00:11:49.842 --> 00:11:51.677
Would have been pretty [bleep]
great right now,

00:11:51.677 --> 00:11:53.879
given that we're going through
a massive healthcare emergency

00:11:53.879 --> 00:11:55.147
in which millions of people

00:11:55.147 --> 00:11:57.449
are also losing
their health insurance.

00:11:57.449 --> 00:11:59.951
Maybe we are finally
all learning now

00:11:59.951 --> 00:12:03.021
that tying your healthcare
to your job was a stupid idea.

00:12:03.021 --> 00:12:05.524
I mean, what do they have to do
with each other anyway?

00:12:05.524 --> 00:12:07.626
If we really wanted
to make healthcare

00:12:07.626 --> 00:12:10.929
commensurate with your job,
then nurses, delivery workers,

00:12:10.929 --> 00:12:13.399
and grocery clerks would get
free gold-plated healthcare

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:16.034
for the rest of their lives
and racist game show hosts

00:12:16.034 --> 00:12:17.369
would have to pay
a million bucks

00:12:17.369 --> 00:12:19.004
to replace every tooth
that falls out.

00:12:19.004 --> 00:12:22.007
-God bless the United Shates.

00:12:22.007 --> 00:12:24.643
-You have to admit, Bernie
fundamentally changed politics.

00:12:24.643 --> 00:12:26.645
And he did it in the course
of like five years.

00:12:26.645 --> 00:12:28.613
Let's just remember how
extraordinary this was.

00:12:28.613 --> 00:12:31.082
I mean, his first campaign
began in 2015

00:12:31.082 --> 00:12:34.219
when he wandered up to
reporters, I guess in a park,

00:12:34.219 --> 00:12:36.622
and told them he was running
for president and also

00:12:36.622 --> 00:12:38.791
that he was too busy
to talk to them.

00:12:38.791 --> 00:12:43.461
-Thank you all very, very much,
whoa, for being out here today.

00:12:43.461 --> 00:12:46.164
Let me just make a brief
comment,

00:12:46.164 --> 00:12:48.200
and I'll be happy
to take a few questions.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.669
We don't have an endless amount
of time. I've got to get back.

00:12:50.669 --> 00:12:53.305
-I'm so bummed we passed up
on the chance for a president

00:12:53.305 --> 00:12:55.941
who hated pomp and circumstance
as much as Bernie did.

00:12:55.941 --> 00:12:59.711
His State of the Unions would
have been 10 minutes tops.

00:12:59.711 --> 00:13:02.047
[ As Sanders ] Please, hold
your applause until the end.

00:13:02.047 --> 00:13:03.748
Or, you know, hold it entirely.

00:13:03.748 --> 00:13:06.685
I don't care much for empty
displays of enthusiasm.

00:13:06.685 --> 00:13:10.856
When old people give standing
ovations, it's very silly.

00:13:10.856 --> 00:13:12.524
[ Normal voice ] I mean,
he walked up to them

00:13:12.524 --> 00:13:14.193
like he had been in that park
all night.

00:13:14.193 --> 00:13:15.794
[ As Sanders ] Get out of here.
You're scaring the birds.

00:13:15.794 --> 00:13:17.629
It's a very delicate ecosystem.

00:13:17.629 --> 00:13:19.999
Also, he personally covered
that podium himself

00:13:19.999 --> 00:13:22.001
and decided to stop
after making the top.

00:13:22.001 --> 00:13:24.569
Who needs a full podium?
It's too ostentatious.

00:13:24.569 --> 00:13:27.305
And in a fitting way, Bernie
bookended his two campaigns

00:13:27.305 --> 00:13:29.207
for president with
an announcement in a park

00:13:29.207 --> 00:13:31.643
and a fiery speech from
the Senate floor last month

00:13:31.643 --> 00:13:34.546
in which he fought to protect
extra pay for workers

00:13:34.546 --> 00:13:36.482
who lost their jobs
due to the pandemic.

00:13:36.482 --> 00:13:40.786
-And now I find that
some of my Republican colleagues

00:13:40.786 --> 00:13:41.820
are very distressed.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:43.422
They are very upset

00:13:43.422 --> 00:13:46.925
that somebody who's making
10, 12 bucks an hour,

00:13:46.925 --> 00:13:50.996
might end up with a paycheck
for four months

00:13:50.996 --> 00:13:53.732
more than they received
last week.

00:13:53.732 --> 00:13:58.237
Oh, my God,
the universe is collapsing.

00:13:58.237 --> 00:14:02.440
Imagine that -- Somebody who's
making 12 bucks an hour

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.209
now, like the rest of us,

00:14:04.209 --> 00:14:07.613
faces an unprecedented
economic crisis

00:14:07.613 --> 00:14:11.316
with the 600 bucks
on top of their normal,

00:14:11.316 --> 00:14:13.518
their regular unemployment
check,

00:14:13.518 --> 00:14:18.123
might be making a few bucks more
for four months.

00:14:18.123 --> 00:14:22.060
Oh, my word!
Will the universe survive?!

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:23.962
-Sarcastic Bernie
is the best Bernie.

00:14:23.962 --> 00:14:25.631
I think it's
his Brooklyn accent.

00:14:25.631 --> 00:14:27.499
He's like an old-timer
working a shift

00:14:27.499 --> 00:14:30.302
at the Park Slope Food Coop
dealing with snooty newcomers.

00:14:30.302 --> 00:14:32.504
"Excuse me, there is no more
organic arugula."

00:14:32.504 --> 00:14:34.406
[ As Sanders ] Oh, my word!

00:14:34.406 --> 00:14:36.875
You have to make your fancy
salads with regular arugula.

00:14:36.875 --> 00:14:41.146
Imagine that. How will
the universe survive?!

00:14:41.146 --> 00:14:44.015
[ Normal voice ] We need
those kinds of major changes

00:14:44.015 --> 00:14:45.183
to deal with
the broken government

00:14:45.183 --> 00:14:46.785
that Trump is currently
exposing.

00:14:46.785 --> 00:14:49.588
He ignored years of warnings
about a possible pandemic,

00:14:49.588 --> 00:14:50.989
lied about it when it arrived,

00:14:50.989 --> 00:14:53.125
forfeited responsibility
to the states,

00:14:53.125 --> 00:14:54.893
pushed an unproven miracle cure,

00:14:54.893 --> 00:14:57.829
and is now asking us to just
forget the whole thing.

00:14:57.829 --> 00:14:59.698
And if you beg him
to provide leadership,

00:14:59.698 --> 00:15:01.033
he responds by saying...

00:15:01.033 --> 00:15:02.534
-I don't think
I'm gonna be doing it.

00:15:02.534 --> 00:15:06.071
-This has been "A Closer Look."
Three?

00:15:06.071 --> 00:15:09.942
♪♪

00:15:09.942 --> 00:15:11.810
City Harvest
is such a great charity,

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:13.145
and now they're working hard

00:15:13.145 --> 00:15:15.313
to support New York City
families who are out of work

00:15:15.313 --> 00:15:17.349
due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

00:15:17.349 --> 00:15:19.918
If you're watching this online,
please hit the "Donate" button,

00:15:19.918 --> 00:15:21.086
give what you can.

00:15:21.086 --> 00:15:23.555
Stay safe. Wash your hands.
We love you.

